<EnglishInstitutionalPage
  title="Mission | Canapalandia"
  description="Canapalandia's editorial mission: independent information, verifiable sources, transparency and useful tools about hemp, CBD and regulation."
  canonical="/en/mission/"
  alternateIt="/chi-siamo/missione/"
  eyebrow="Our mission"
  heading="Understand hemp better, without slogans or shortcuts"
  lead="We want to make hemp regulation, research, markets and culture easier to understand, offering verifiable information and practical tools without turning information into a commercial or therapeutic promise."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Inform before persuading</h2>
    <p>Hemp, CBD and cannabis light are subjects where politics, science, markets and communication easily overlap. Our mission is to reduce confusion: explain what we know, what we do not know and which sources readers can use to go deeper.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Editorial principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sources before opinions:</strong> official documents, studies, court decisions and verifiable data have priority.</li>
      <li><strong>Context:</strong> an isolated sentence or sensational headline is rarely enough to explain a complex issue.</li>
      <li><strong>Updates:</strong> regulation and research change; sensitive content should be reviewed when substantial new information emerges.</li>
      <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> advertising, affiliate relationships and sponsored content must be recognisable.</li>
      <li><strong>Caution:</strong> we do not turn preliminary studies, testimonials or hypotheses into promises of effectiveness.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>We are not a shop</h2>
    <p>The current Canapalandia is an editorial project. We do not directly sell products, manage orders or replace the producer, laboratory, doctor, pharmacist or legal professional.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>From information to tools</h2>
    <p>When useful, we turn explanations into practical tools. <a href="/en/lab/">Canapalandia Lab</a>, for example, helps readers interpret selected information in a COA certificate through automatic rules without sending the document to Canapalandia's servers.</p>
    <p>The tool translates recognised data but does not make determinations about a product's legality, safety or quality.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>A community that can correct us</h2>
    <p>Independence does not mean infallibility. If you find an error, a missing source or content that has become outdated, report it through the <a href="/en/contact/">Contact page</a>. Well-founded corrections are part of editorial work, not something to hide.</p>
  </section>
</EnglishInstitutionalPage>
